 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 532574,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Find the area of a regular hexagon with side length of 5 and apothem equal to 4.3.\n<br>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/8ec810d482ec38dd.png\" alt=\"A hexagon. Each side measures 5 centimeters. The apothem is marked 4.3 centimeters.\">\n",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The apothem of a regular polygon is a line segment that starts at the center and is perpendicular to a side. The area of a regular polygon with apothem <i>a</i> and perimeter <i>p</i> is <span data-math=\"A = \\frac{1}{2}ap\"></span>.</p>\n<p>A regular hexagon has six sides of equal length. Therefore, the perimeter is:</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"p = 6(5{\\text{ cm)  =  30 cm}}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"A = \\frac{1}{2}ap = \\frac{1}{2}\\left( {4.3{\\text{ cm}}} \\right)\\left( {{\\text{30 cm}}} \\right) = 64.5{\\text{ c}}{{\\text{m}}^2}\"></span></p>\n<p>The area is 64.5 square centimeters.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"64.5\\,{\\text{c}}{{\\text{m}}^2}\">64.5\\,{\\text{c}}{{\\text{m}}^2}</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
